# Verify CI after every push or merge

Pushing or merging is not done until the relevant GitHub Actions runs finish green.

## Required after `git push` or merging a PR

1. Identify the branch/PR and the workflows that must pass for that change.
   - Default for PRs / `master`: `ci` (js, e2e, rust, ios-project, nix).
   - Pushes to `master` that touch Apple/release paths also require `ios-testflight` green — not only `ci`.
2. Watch until completion (`gh pr checks <n> --watch` or `gh run watch <id>`). Do not stop at "jobs started" or "most jobs passed".
3. If anything fails: read the failed job logs, fix, push again, and re-watch to green. Do not leave a red tip on `master`.
4. Only then report success to the user, including the run conclusions that matter (especially `ios-testflight` when it ran).

## Do not

- Merge and walk away while `ios-testflight` (or any required workflow) is still pending.
- Treat "PR CI green" as enough when `master` also runs TestFlight upload after merge.
- Declare the task finished while the latest run on the pushed tip is red or still in progress.
